        <item>
            <title>1.5.6</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 10 Jul 2026 08:48:21 +0900</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>38</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.5.6</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h3>Added</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>New Text Document.</b> Right-click the empty area of a folder (or use File ▸ New Text Document) to create an empty `.txt` file with its name ready to edit — Windows Explorer's "New ▸ Text Document", including collision-safe naming ("New Text Document 2.txt") and undo that removes the file only while it is still empty.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Fixed</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Creating a folder or text file in symlinked locations (such as /tmp)</b> now opens the inline name editor.<b> The just-created item could fail to</b> match the listing in such folders, so the name editor silently never appeared; it now matches reliably, and a missed attempt retries instead of giving up.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
